<title>ROMANIA: Bucharest bourse gets one more listing.</title>
<headline>Bucharest bourse gets one more listing.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bucharest stock exchange said on Monday its total listings would rise to 37 as a new company joins in trading later this week.</p>
<p>A bourse statement said shares of Somes SA pulp and paper maker would be traded from Wednesday on the second tier.</p>
<p>The newcomer has a share capital of 169.37 billion lei in shares with a nominal value of 25,000 lei each.</p>
<p>Its majority 69.99 percent stockholder is the State Ownership Fund. An investment company holds 21.16 percent and other shareholders have the rest.</p>
<p>The Bucharest stock exchange now lists 36 stocks. Four are on the first tier -- two chemical plants and two pharmaceuticals companies.</p>
<p>-- Luli Popescu, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
